  "flow_summary": "The interviewer successfully completed the intake and managed the patient's somewhat imprecise communication style. However, the system frequently used a repetitive, mechanical prompt ('在我们继续之前，您能回答上面的问题吗？') even when the patient had already provided the information or was in the middle of a natural conversation, which felt redundant and slightly robotic.",
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "redundant_questioning",
      "evidence": "The interviewer repeatedly appended '在我们继续之前，您能回答上面的问题吗？' to almost every turn, even when the patient had just provided a clear answer or was clearly engaged in the process."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "mechanical_flow",
      "evidence": "The transition to the PHQ-9 and GAD-7 sections felt rigid, and the system's insistence on repeating the full question text when the patient expressed slight confusion (e.g., '我不太明白，能换个说法问吗？') was helpful but the overall interaction felt more like a script-reading exercise than a clinical interview."
    }
  ],
